The `focusOnUIElement` call with `poll: true` always returns a `Promise<boolean>` (per the comment and implementation on the existing close-path just above), but the result is dropped here with no `.then()` handler. The close-path (lines 372–381) uses the established pattern:
```ts
(fullAPI.focusOnUIElement(...) as Promise<boolean>).then((success) => {
  if (success === false) { document.body.focus(); }
});
```
The open-path should follow the same convention. If focus polling times out (resolves `false`), there is currently no fallback and the user's focus silently stays wherever it was. Apply the same `.then()` + `document.body.focus()` fallback used by the close-path.
